QTranslate for Debian
=====================

Build from the source tree with the command the user uses:

  DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS="parallel=$(nproc) nocheck nodoc" dpkg-buildpackage -rfakeroot -us -uc

There is no trailing ".": dpkg-buildpackage 1.21.22 on Astra Linux 1.8.7
rejects a "." argument ("unknown option or argument ."), and "." is not an
argument of dpkg-buildpackage.

The artifacts land in the parent directory:

  qtranslate_0.12.0_amd64.deb
  qtranslate_0.12.0.dsc
  qtranslate_0.12.0.tar.xz

DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS:

  nocheck        skip the test suite.  The copyright and changelog are
                 installed either way.
  nodoc          skip README.Debian.  The copyright and changelog are still
                 installed.
  parallel=N     pass N to the CMake/Ninja build.

Without nocheck, debian/rules runs the suite under xvfb-run.  On Astra Linux
1.8.7 the passive-grab X11 tests (tst_hotkeymanager_x11 and
tst_hotkey_selection_x11) need a trusted-client entry for their
build/debian/tests/... paths:

  /etc/X11/trusted.d/qtranslate
    /path/to/qtranslate/build/debian/tests/tst_hotkeymanager_x11(KBD_R)
    /path/to/qtranslate/build/debian/tests/tst_hotkey_selection_x11(KBD_R)

  sudo /usr/bin/fly-set-execid.sh

The nocheck build does not need this entry.
